{"q": 19935, "quiz": 1638, "obj": "P1.COMPETITOR", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "How does Kai-Kai help Brownie before the winter?", "why": "في الفقرة أفعال عدّة تتنافس، وأكثرها لبراوني؛ والمطلوب فعل الغراب: «Kai-Kai helped him by throwing some walnuts down.»", "opts": [{"t": "He makes a small den in the ground.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "He drops walnuts from the tree to the ground.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "He picks up the walnuts from the ground.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "He makes a nest for Brownie in the tree.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19936, "quiz": 1638, "obj": "P2.MOTIVE", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "Why does Brownie dig a small den in the ground?", "why": "الدافع من قوله وفعله في الفقرة نفسها: «I shall make a small den in the ground and bury some walnuts in it. I can use them in the winters.»", "opts": [{"t": "He wants to hide there from Kai-Kai.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "He wants to keep walnuts there for the winter.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "He wants to sleep there in the snow.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "He wants a new nest under the tree.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19937, "quiz": 1638, "obj": "P2.WORD_CONTEXT", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "What does \"interdependence\" mean in this book?", "why": "المعنى من الجملة نفسها: «Depending on one another for living and growing is called interdependence.»", "opts": [{"t": "Animals store their food before the winter.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "A tree makes new walnuts every year.", "dx": "MIX", "key": false}, {"t": "Plants help animals, and animals help plants.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "Plants give out oxygen in the forest.", "dx": "PART", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19938, "quiz": 1638, "obj": "P3.CHANGE", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "In October, Walnut is worried about Brownie's food. How are things different in the winter?", "why": "التغيّر بين أول القصة وشتائها: كان القلق «What will you eat in the winters?» ثم بعد التخزين «Brownie was safe and happy as he had plenty to eat.»", "opts": [{"t": "Brownie is hungry and has no walnuts.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}, {"t": "Kai-Kai and Brownie live in one nest.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "Brownie is safe and has plenty to eat.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "Walnut makes new walnuts in the snow.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}]},
{"q": 19939, "quiz": 1638, "obj": "P4.WORD_CHOICE", "kind": "mcq", "was": "sentence", "body": "In one sentence, Walnut uses the words \"tiny\" and \"huge\" about Brownie's help. Why does the writer put these two words together?", "why": "الكاتب جمع الضدّين ليُبرز أن العمل الصغير أثره كبير: «Your tiny hands will make a huge difference.»", "opts": [{"t": "To show the hard life of a small animal.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "To show the sad life of a very big tree.", "dx": "JUMP", "key": false}, {"t": "To show the big work of a small animal.", "dx": null, "key": true}, {"t": "To show the big hands of a small animal.", "dx": "REV", "key": false}]},
